/E (Chemical hazards are prevalent across industries, with the increasing use of complex and newly developed chemicals. This category includes over 12,000 toxic substances that pose significant risks to human health and safety. Exposure to these chemicals can result in acute effects such as poisoning, severe discomfort, or immediate health deterioration. Additionally, prolonged exposure may lead to chronic diseases, including cancer and pneumoconiosis.)
