4134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (An MATERIAL SAFETY DATA SHEETS \(MSDS\) applies to a chemical product as a whole and provides non-confidential information regarding its composition and ingredients. Suppliers are required to provide a complete, up-to-date MSDS that contains relevant safety, health, and situations that may arise in the workplace. The responsibility lies with the user to assess risks based on the specific conditions under which the chemical product is used and ensure that workers are appropriately informed about the relevant hazards in their environment. The MSDS, therefore, forms only a part of the information needed to establish a comprehensive safety program. While a single MSDS may be produced for a mixture, detailing individual ingredients may not be necessary unless it is useful for the workplace. In such cases, information on each ingredient should be provided. An MSDS shall provide the relevant information about a chemical product, in following 16 section headings. Text of the section headings, numbering and sequence shall not be altered. The section headings are given: )
/K [2]
/Pg 1292 0 R
>>
endobj
